Hi all,

I updated a laptop (Lenovo R61 7732-CTO) running Debian/lenny from 2.6.27.19
to 2.6.29.4 and noticed X was no longer working (I rarely fire up X on it, so
didn't notice until recently).

The failure mode was similar to when KMS is enabled, but .config did not
have KMS in it.  Bisecting it down gave me:

commit ab657db12d7020629f26f30d287558a8d0e32b41
Author: Eric Anholt <eric@anholt.net>
Date:   Fri Jan 23 12:57:47 2009 -0800

    drm/i915: Set up an MTRR covering the GTT at driver load.
    
    We'd love to just be using PAT, but even on chips with PAT it gets disabled
    sometimes due to an errata.  It would probably be better to have pat_enabled
    exported and only bother with this when !pat_enabled.
    
    Signed-off-by: Eric Anholt <eric@anholt.net>
    Signed-off-by: Dave Airlie <airlied@linux.ie>



